  "question": {
    "text": "Two bar magnets oscillate in a horizontal plane in earth&#39;s magnetic field with time periods of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>respectively. If their moments of inertia are in the ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;then the ratio of their magnetic moments will be&nbsp;",
